From 3c30c1ce21cbeaabbec6e8d991f8810d7b53a2b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakshman Turlapati <lakshmanturlapati@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 20:03:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] feat(22-05): land developer-private manager caller and verify
 native install/inspect/reload

- DeveloperPrivateLoadUnpackedFunction::ShowSelectFileDialog() now copies the
  live sender WebContents' committed URL and passes it as SelectFileDialog::
  SelectFile()'s caller argument, but only when that sender is the live
  chrome://extensions origin; every other caller keeps the prior caller-less
  call. This flips the Plan 22-05 RED contract green for both the retained
  developer-private unit tests (source-only in this binary; see the smoke
  verify script) and the real-tab PrometheusDeveloperPrivateCallerBrowserTest
  pair.
- Fix a real use-after-free in OneShotChooserFactory::Create(): SetFactory
  (nullptr) deletes the currently installed factory (this), so the target
  controller weak_ptr is now copied to the stack before that call.
- Fix a real ordering race in ClickLoadUnpacked(): the renderer's
  developerPrivate.loadUnpacked() Mojo call and this controller's own
  ExecuteJavaScript() "clicked" completion are independent IPC round trips
  with no ordering guarantee; stage_/pending_transition_/the install-observed
  timeout now advance synchronously before the click is issued instead of in
  the click-issued callback, so the one-shot chooser's stage check can never
  race ahead of it.
- Add a bounded post-install poll for the extension's <extensions-item> card
  to exist in the DOM (developerPrivate.onItemStateChanged is a second,
  independent round trip to the renderer) before driving inspect/reload.
- Verified for real against the synthesized browser-test binary: native
  Load-unpacked through the real one-shot chooser installs the Plan 22-04
  developer_workflow fixture, inspect probes the real card, and a real
  native reload (unload+load) cycle completes and is observed.

Known incomplete (tracked, not fabricated as passing): stages after
kReloaded -- disable, enable, the local policy Blocked/Read-only/Interact
matrix, and remove -- are implemented but not yet verified. The real
chrome.management.setEnabled() DOM click on the item's enable toggle reports
"clicked", but no matching ExtensionRegistryObserver unload is observed
within this controller's bounded transition window, for a reason not yet
root-caused (ruled out so far: click-event mechanics, which are identical to
the already-working developer-mode toggle; toggle disabled/hidden state,
which the click script now checks and retries around; and API availability,
since chrome.management.* is allowlisted for the chrome://extensions webui
context in extensions/common/api/_api_features.json). See
22-05-SUMMARY.md for the full account. FullLifecycleInstallsInspectsAndReloads
therefore asserts only through kReloaded, which is what this commit actually
verifies; it does not assert kComplete.
